# LINE ENDINGS, DECLARED - because the alternative is a permanently dirty tree.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so git rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout.
# Every generator here writes LF (Python, opened with newline=""), and CI runs
# on Linux. So a file that is checked out and then regenerated comes back
# different in every byte that ends a line, and `git status` has been showing
# tracker/analysis.js and tracker/splits.js as modified after every single
# build - with an empty diff under --ignore-cr-at-eol.
#
# That is worse than untidy. A permanently dirty tree is a tree nobody reads,
# and it has already cost one `git checkout` that had to be talked through
# before it was safe to run.
#
# Declaring the endings here beats autocrlf, so the bytes on disk match the
# bytes in the index and the two stop arguing.

# Everything this repository generates or ships to the browser.
*.js        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf

# Images and fonts are bytes, and must never be touched.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
